  "completeCard": "---\nkanji: 鈍\ntitle: dull; blunt\njlpt: 2\ntags: [jlpt-n2, grade-8, structure-unclassified]\nstrokes: 12\nradical: 金\nradicalNumber: 167\nonyomi: [ドン]\nkunyomi: [にぶ.い, にぶ.る, にぶ-, なま.る, なまく.ら]\ndistractors: [純, 線, 銀]\n---\n\n# 鈍 — dull; blunt\n\n**Strokes:** 12 · **Key (radical):** 金 (no. 167) · **JLPT:** N2 (community list)\n\n## Meaning and origin\n\n鈍 concerns bluntness, dullness or slow responsiveness. 鈍い is an adjective, 鈍る a verb for becoming dull, and 鈍化 names a dulling or slowing process.\n\n**Modern-shape mnemonic, not etymology:** Imagine the rounded 屯-shaped strokes beside 金 as a tool whose edge is no longer sharp. This is only a modern-shape mnemonic.\n\nThe canonical radical 金 is the narrow left-hand part.\n\n## Readings\n\n| Reading | Type | Typical words |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| ドン | on | 鈍化 どんか - becoming dull; slowing down |\n| にぶ.い | kun | [鈍い](../words/鈍い.md) にぶい - dull; blunt; slow to perceive |\n| にぶ.る | kun | 鈍る にぶる - become blunt; grow dull |\n| にぶ- | kun | 鈍らす にぶらす - blunt; dull; にぶ occurs as a bound stem |\n| なま.る | kun | 鈍る なまる - become blunt; grow dull |\n| なまく.ら | kun | 鈍ら なまくら - blunt; dull (usually written in kana) |\n\n## Common words\n\n- [鈍い](../words/鈍い.md) にぶい - dull; blunt; slow to perceive\n- [のろい](../words/のろい.md) のろい - slow; slow-witted; usually kana, also written 鈍い\n- 鈍化 どんか - becoming dull; slowing down\n- 鈍痛 どんつう - dull pain\n\n## Notes\n\n- 鈍る has both にぶる and なまる in the inspected family without a rarity flag on either. Both are intransitive; 鈍らす にぶらす is a separate transitive verb. Dictionary recognition does not establish equal frequency.\n- The source notation なまく.ら gives the complete word 鈍ら なまくら, with written ら after 鈍. JMdict marks its blunt-edge sense usually written in kana. It is a na-adjective, unlike 鈍い.\n- にぶ- is retained as a bound source reading and illustrated inside the complete word 鈍らす, not taught as a free-standing word.\n- A separate usually-kana entry records [のろい](../words/のろい.md), also written 鈍い. The [鈍い](../words/鈍い.md) article teaches にぶい; that additional word identity does not change the pinned character-reading list or add a new reading row here.\n\nMetadata: [KANJIDIC2](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/KANJIDIC_Project), 2026-10-21 snapshot. Word pairs: [JMdict](https://www.edrdg.org/wiki/index.php/JMdict-EDICT_Dictionary_Project), entries 1457580, 1457660, 1582430, 1582440, 1900190, 2009300, 2838553.\n",
